ction both by  individuals and by  by units and most of this hasn't been  documented so i go into it in the book  in significant detail i'll just mention  a couple examples  november 25th  1962 south vietnamese army  force of about a hundred at the outpost  of fort cha  is attacked by uh up to a thousand enemy  soldiers  north korea soldiers  the government forces have prepared  their defenses very well and they've got  some howitzers in the area that they're  that they've lined up anticipating the  successful or the enemy attack  and uh the defense proves to be  extremely defective excuse me effective  the vietcong leave 124 dead on the  battlefield certainly they took some  more people with them  government's total casualties are 10  wounded no dead  something we don't hear about another  example may 11th 1965 at song bay  just a handful of us advisors in  advisory compound  uh under attack by two vietcong  battalions that are in possession of  eight heavy weapons companies they  managed to hold them off until they  exhaust most of their heavy ammunition  which again heavy weaponry very  important by this time  and by the next morning the south  vietnamese regiment comes in and  dislodges the vietcong from song bay  individual  who really distinguishes himself one of  many during this period is marvin  shields  he's present at the attack on dungswa on  june 10th of 65  when two vietcong regiments attack the  town  they overrun a lot of position  government positions  but the government headquarters and the  advisory compound or excuse me special  forces advisory compound are still  intact  and shields is seen and there's lots of  documentation of this jumping from  position to position  to distribute ammunition to  help the wounded and to fire at the  enemy  and he shot twice during that period  including one that takes out a good part  of his face  but at one point there's an enemy  machine gun that's put up that is a  grave threat to their position  and he's vol